---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '22 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Delete your Plinth account"
  description="How to delete your Plinth account and what happens to your data.">
  <section class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Delete your Plinth account</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      You can delete your Plinth account from inside the app at any time. You don't need to
      contact us, and there's nothing to wait for — it happens immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>How to delete your account</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open Plinth and sign in</li>
      <li>Go to the <strong>Profile</strong> tab</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Account</strong></li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Delete account</strong></li>
      <li>Type <strong>DELETE</strong> to confirm</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
    <p>Everything below is removed straight away and cannot be recovered:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, email address and profile picture</li>
      <li>Saved recipes, including any you imported yourself</li>
      <li>Planned meals in your calendar</li>
      <li>Shopping list items you added</li>
      <li>Shopping lists you created, including for anyone you shared them with</li>
      <li>Your membership of shopping lists other people created — their lists stay with them</li>
      <li>Your subscription record</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is kept, and for how long</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Payment records.</strong> Purchases are handled by Google Play, not by us, and
        Google keeps its own transaction records for tax and accounting reasons. Deleting your
        Plinth account does not delete them. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Crash reports.</strong> If the app crashed before you deleted your account, the
        report may still exist for up to 90 days. It contains a technical trace and an
        anonymous account identifier, never your name or email address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Recipe data.</strong> Recipes themselves come from Spoonacular and are shared
        between everyone using Plinth. They were never yours in the first place, so nothing
        personal is held there.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cancelling a subscription</h2>
    <p>
      Deleting your account does not automatically cancel a Google Play subscription. Cancel it
      in the Play Store first: open the Play Store, tap your profile picture, then
      <strong>Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions → Plinth Premium → Cancel</strong>.
      You keep premium access until the end of the period you've already paid for.
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting some data without deleting your account</h2>
    <p>
      You don't have to delete everything to remove something. Inside the app you can delete
      individual saved recipes, clear your shopping list, remove planned meals, leave a shared
      list, and change or remove your profile picture — all without closing your account.
    </p>

    <h2>Need help?</h2>
    <p>
      If you can't access your account and want it deleted, email
      <a href="mailto:plinthrecipes@gmail.com">plinthrecipes@gmail.com</a> from the address on
      the account and we'll handle it for you.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
